※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4250
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4250 LANG_TEXT_NOT_BYTES

※ Text is made of bytes, so bytes are what `⎕text` checks and copies: a `u8⟦⟧`, an array
※ of `u8` whose type says its shape, or a list of them.  An array of wider numbers is not
※ the bytes of anything -- which of its bytes come first is the machine's business -- and
※ nothing else is either.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let wide: u16⟦2⟧ = ⟦0x6869u16, 0x2121u16⟧ in ⎕static
    let t: str = ⎕text(wide) ?? ""
    if t = "hi!!": 0u6 else: 1u6
